    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's easy to say it's \"non-linear\" when you're just observing it from the outside. but when you actually run the numbers on the resources spent, the time lost, and the wreckage left behind... the pattern is undeniable. it’s not just a \"feeling.\" it’s a calculation. it feels like i'm fighting against the physics of my own existence. how can you call it a \"reset\" when the math just says there's nothing left to reset? it feels like i've reached the point of diminishing returns on life itself.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
